            <li>Your name, address, telephone number, and email;</li>
            <li>A statement consenting to jurisdiction of federal court in your area;</li>
            <li>A statement that you accept service of process.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Repeat Infringers</h2>
        <p>Lucahman maintains a policy of terminating the accounts of repeat copyright infringers in its sole discretion. Users who repeatedly infringe copyrights will have their access revoked.</p>
        
        <h2>Response Timeline</h2>
        <p>We will respond to valid DMCA notices within ten (10) business days of receipt. Upon receipt of a valid counter-notice, we will provide it to the party who submitted the original notice and will restore access to the material within ten (10) business days, unless the copyright holder files suit or requests expedited action.</p>
        
        <h2>Legal Liability</h2>
        <p><strong>False Claims:</strong> Making false statements in a DMCA notice or counter-notice under penalty of perjury can result in liability for damages, including costs and attorneys' fees. False claims may constitute perjury under 18 U.S.C. § 1621.</p>
        
